7
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:25,440
(House on fire)

8
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,800
Dad!

9
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,560
Dad!

10
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:50,280
(Dad's so happy
you finally became a cop.)

11
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,600
(James can be hotheaded sometimes.)

12
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:59,840
(But it also makes James
braver than most.)

13
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,160
(As long as you know
you're doing the right thing,)

14
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,920
(you'll have nothing to fear.)

15
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,640
(James, don't ever change.)

16
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,960
(Dad is proud of you.)

17
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:30,760
=Nour=
(A WeTV Original Series)

18
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:38,920
What are you doing?

19
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:48,800
Hey, Inspector.

20
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,960
Did you find

21
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,320
what you were looking for?

22
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,440
How much do you know about this case?

23
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,760
Where did you get all this?

24
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,080
Tell me the truth. Now.

25
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,960
The truth is, you had no right
to break into my car.

26
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,960
Or should I report you for misconduct?

27
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,720
Spare me the discipline bullshit.

28
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:42,040
You're no better than me.

29
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,920
I'm warning you.

30
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,880
If you want us to work together,

31
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,520
don't cross the line.

32
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,320
Hey, let's talk this out.

33
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:07,600
A female student was brutally murdered
at a prestigious university.

34
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,720
Her boyfriend is the prime suspect.

35
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,560
Police believe he may be the killer.

36
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,760
A breakup may be the motive.

37
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:17,440
Police are still seeking
eyewitnesses for the case

38
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,520
What exactly happened?

39
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,120
I don't know what it was, but...

40
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:25,080
it definitely wasn't human.

41
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,680
I was arguing with Mint.

42
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,640
Then suddenly,

43
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,920
Mint disappeared.

44
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:33,360
When I turned back,
it was attacking Mint.

45
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,680
Then it turned and tried to kill me.

46
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,160
After that,

47
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,040
it vanished, leaving marks
on Mint's neck.

48
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:46,400
These wounds don't look human-inflicted.

49
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,160
It's Nour. Yes.

50
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:49,840
The Nour from all those internet posts.

51
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,960
Nour must've done it.

52
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,360
What are you talking about?

53
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:56,560
I'm telling you, Nour doesn't exist.

54
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:59,080
The killer is what's real.

55
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,760
Officer.

56
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,960
I know it's hard to believe,

57
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,960
but I'm not lying.

58
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:07,960
Please believe me.

59
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,480
I only believe what I see
with my own eyes.

60
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,880
And what I see is

61
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:18,280
you are...

62
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,280
Time to tell the truth.

63
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:25,480
(Pathology Room)
Ji.

64
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,040
(Forensic Lab)
How did Mint die?

65
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,240
Was it really Ping who killed her?

66
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,640
Mim, go home first.

67
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:32,920
Don't hang around here.

68
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,880
Take your friend home too.

69
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:38,040
Ji, go easy on my friend.

70
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,960
How would that help him?

71
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,360
Please leave.

72
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:46,800
Come on, Ink.

73
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,760
What's wrong with you?

74
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,240
What did you say?

75
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:00,760
What did James do?

76
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,760
- Your turn, Doctor.
- Okay.

77
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:09,400
Sorry. There's a lunatic at the station.

78
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:17,800
Inspector, you're finally here.

79
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:20,520
We tried everything
to stop Inspector James.

80
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,480
He even threw me out.

81
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,440
Step back.

82
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,560
Who said you could question him first?

83
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,920
One second.

84
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,600
You took forever to get here.

85
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,400
I was just speeding things up.

86
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,600
You know what?

87
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:50,040
This suspect

88
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,560
told the same Nour story as Joe.

89
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,880
This wasn't done by a human.

90
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,600
Outside.

91
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,360
How can you say that?

92
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:01,480
Didn't you send the case
to the Special Investigation Unit?

93
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,800
I know.

94
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,960
If you hadn't made it a special case,

95
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,720
Dr. Jirat wouldn't have called you
to examine the body.

96
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,200
Do you know that

97
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,240
during interrogations,

98
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,480
they torture people into talking?

99
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:27,560
Isn't that illegal?

100
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:30,960
Out here in the sticks,

101
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,400
what good is the law?

102
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,640
One more thing.

103
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,040
You weren't honest with me either.

104
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:38,600
Why should I care?

105
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,440
But everything I said was true.

106
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:43,480
I really didn't hurt Mint.

107
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,080
The one you should fear

108
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,440
isn't me.

109
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,800
It's the man behind the glass.

110
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,240
Inspector Ken.

111
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,520
He's ten times scarier than me.

112
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,440
See this wound?

113
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,080
See it?

114
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:07,160
Yes.

115
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:08,640
Good.

116
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,560
Inspector Ken gave me this

117
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,640
just because I provoked him.

118
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,160
Imagine what he'd do to a brat like you.

119
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:22,600
Inspector Ken

120
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:25,200
likes to keep to himself.

121
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,920
He's not exactly friendly,

122
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:30,040
and he's impossible to read.

123
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,280
Watch him all you want,

124
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:33,920
but you'll never read him.

125
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,320
Worse still,

126
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,760
he's completely heartless.

127
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:40,560
No heart.

128
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,360
No feelings at all.

129
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:48,040
He won't go easy on you like I did.

130
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,520
So one last chance.

131
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,680
Tell me the truth,

132
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,520
or should I bring Inspector Ken in?

133
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:56,040
Okay! Okay!

134
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,720
Can I have my phone?

135
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:01,040
The photos and

136
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,080
everything else are on it.

137
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,000
I'll show you.

138
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:05,360
I'm sorry.

139
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,800
That's more like it, kid.

140
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,000
Give it to me.

141
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,760
This is yours, right?

142
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,760
Yes.

143
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,120
Look, your phone just arrived.

144
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,000
Let me introduce you two.

145
00:09:39,160 --> 00:09:40,720
This is Inspector Ken.

146
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:43,480
You said you wouldn't
bring Inspector Ken in.

147
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:44,800
What did you want to show me?

148
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:47,400
The private album.

149
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:01,880
Give me.

150
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:03,680
Password?

151
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,800
Six fives.

152
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,200
Six fives.

153
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,240
Oh. A sex tape.

154
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,600
What's this video about?

155
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,760
Okay, I lied about one thing.

156
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,320
I threatened to leak the video
to blackmail Mint.

157
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:25,240
But I didn't lie about anything else.

158
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,560
Please let me go.

159
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:28,360
I'm sorry.

160
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,240
That means the real killer
is still out there.

161
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,800
I'll question witnesses
and gather evidence.

162
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,400
I can't work with someone I don't trust.

163
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:47,920
Neither can I.

164
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:48,800
Fine by me.

165
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,680
I do things my own way.

166
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,080
I don't need your help.

167
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:54,800
From now on,

168
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,760
we'll work the case separately.

169
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:07,480
Ink, can you tell me
what happened that day?

170
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:09,160
That day,

171
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,160
we were sitting around talking.

172
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,960
Then Mint came over.

173
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:15,120
She seemed about to break up with Ping.

174
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,960
She kept complaining

175
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,560
that they'd been fighting lately.

176
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,760
(If it never meant anything,
it might as well never have existed.)

177
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,840
(Let me be your sunshine every day)

178
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,880
I saw Ping ask Mint to talk in private.

179
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:30,680
Things looked tense.

180
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,840
I was afraid they'd argue on campus,

181
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,840
but Mint said she'd be fine.

182
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,480
So I let her go talk to Ping.

183
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,640
You know,

184
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:48,280
when I looked back, Mint was gone.

185
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:50,960
Then I heard Mint scream.

186
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,800
I ran over to see what happened.

187
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:56,680
Inspector.

188
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,840
Dr. Jirat has an autopsy update.

189
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,640
What did he find?

190
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,920
Under the

191
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,600
fingernail.

192
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,800
Right here.

193
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,440
Give it a try. First task on the job.

194
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,240
Go on. Try it.

195
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,160
Mm-hmm.

196
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:50,600
- Done.
- Good job.

197
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,240
I knew you had it in you.

198
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,400
That wasn't good at all, Doctor.

199
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:56,760
That alone

200
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:58,240
had me shaking.

201
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,320
Go put it away.

202
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,080
Doctor, this is...

203
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,880
My new assistant.

204
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,080
Do you remember Chita?

205
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,880
Assistant doesn't need to hear this.

206
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,840
Fine.

207
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,560
You can step out now.

208
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,160
Go on.

209
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,720
The grip crushed her neck.

210
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:30,640
Whoever did it

211
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,280
must've lost control.

212
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,480
Um...

213
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:36,840
You mean

214
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:38,960
it wasn't done on purpose?

215
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,240
With an attack like this,

216
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,440
the killer was either starving

217
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,120
or new at this.

218
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:50,680
Could it be

219
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:53,640
here for the same thing as you?

220
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:00,640
By the way, Chita found

221
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,600
some tissue fragments and gray fibers.

222
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:06,680
Both probably came from the killer.

223
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:08,880
Chita again.

224
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,440
You really like your
new assistant, don't you?

225
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,240
He got in through proper channels.

226
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,680
He had a real interview.
No one pulled strings.

227
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:16,560
Um...

228
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,200
I haven't said anything yet.

229
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:21,560
Yes.

230
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:22,680
Yes, Doctor.

231
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,480
Dr. Ji.

232
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,240
I'm sure you know

233
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,240
what you can tell him

234
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:30,800
and what you can't.

235
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:33,600
Yes, Doctor.

236
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:35,800
Don't forget the DNA test.

237
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:38,200
See if it matches the suspect.

238
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,760
Yes.

239
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,120
(Inspector)

240
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,800
(Ping's phone is missing.)

241
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,720
(I tracked it through the Meta app.)

242
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,120
(The real killer may have taken it.)

243
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,440
Tangme, where is it now?

244
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:01,960
(Near the victim's university, I think.)

245
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,200
Did you bring the phone?

246
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,400
Didn't I tell you?

247
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,440
I'll investigate this my way.

248
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:35,240
Stay out of my way, okay?

249
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,680
(Please keep quiet)

250
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:38,840
Give me the phone.

251
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:42,200
No. Why are you taking my phone?

252
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:45,840
It's evidence.

253
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:47,000
Give it to me.

254
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,440
See that person sitting alone?

255
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:56,920
I think that's Ink.

256
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,240
Witnesses at the scene said

257
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,520
they were all friends.

258
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:05,080
Know what's strange?

259
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,120
The day the body was found,

260
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,800
Ink and Moe were there too.

261
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,320
That's why I think

262
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,720
Ink could be the killer.

263
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,000
You don't believe me?

264
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,240
Let me show you something.

265
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,280
I got what I came for.

266
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:24,440
Do whatever you want.

267
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,240
What's your problem, Inspector?

268
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:29,720
Let go.

269
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,600
I'm here to help with the case.

270
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:33,040
I'm trying to help you.

271
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,040
You...

272
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,600
Let go.

273
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,240
Hey!

274
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:39,920
The case is going nowhere

275
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,680
because you're always so slow.

276
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,000
I said, let go.

277
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,240
Give me the phone.

278
00:16:57,920 --> 00:16:59,400
How about we call a truce?

279
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,760
I wasn't fighting you.

280
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:01,960
Fine. Whatever.

281
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:04,440
Let's just work this case together.

282
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:05,680
Just for today.

283
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:08,000
After today,

284
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,360
we work alone.

285
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:14,440
Then you need to tell me
everything you know.

286
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:18,320
Deal.

287
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:21,360
Deal.

288
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,800
Inspector, look at this.

289
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:48,560
A bracelet.

290
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:49,920
What is it?

291
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:50,880
Hmm.

292
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,520
Now look at the video.

293
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,080
My guess is

294
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,080
Ink and Ping

295
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:05,560
used to date.

296
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,600
Motive?

297
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:12,880
Maybe

298
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,360
Ink

299
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,200
still wanted Ping for herself.

300
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:20,440
Then Ping tried to get back with Mint,
who was in the same friend group.

301
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,720
She got jealous

302
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,240
and killed Mint.

303
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,480
What is it, Inspector?

304
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,800
We found a gray fiber

305
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,880
under the victim's fingernail.

306
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,360
Inspector.

307
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:41,760
I have an idea.

308
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:48,680
More than ten minutes costs extra.

309
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,440
I'll pay.

310
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,200
Give that.

311
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,600
I'll take this one. I'm bigger.

312
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,640
You take that one.

313
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,280
What're you staring at?

314
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:03,880
Turn around.

315
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:08,800
Hey.

316
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:10,800
It's too cramped. Move over.

317
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,240
You think I want to be
pressed against you?

318
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:15,920
Move over.

319
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,080
Oh, come on.

320
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,520
Your skin's really soft.

321
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,600
Have you ever been in a fight?

322
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:33,520
How is your skin this soft?

323
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,240
Hurry up and change.

324
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,840
Why are you so embarrassed?

325
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:39,320
We're both cops.

326
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:41,960
You think I want to see you naked?

327
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,080
Excuse me.

328
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,040
Um...

329
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:41,760
Could you do me a favor?

330
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:43,800
Can I borrow your phone?

331
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:45,560
It's just that

332
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,480
my phone camera's broken.

333
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:49,360
Could I use yours

334
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:50,600
to photograph the textbook,

335
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:52,520
then AirDrop the photos to my phone?

336
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:56,280
Sure. Give me a second.

337
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,960
These are the same notes from class.

338
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:02,760
Exactly. I need these notes.

339
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:04,160
Here.

340
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,040
Hey.

341
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:08,840
I...

342
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,720
accidentally locked it.

343
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,040
Can you unlock it for me?

344
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:13,240
Sure.

345
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,200
There.

346
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,160
Thank you.

347
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:32,520
You might as well take it home.

348
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,120
Sorry.

349
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:36,360
Here.

350
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,840
By the way,

351
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,040
what's your name?

352
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:45,440
I'm Ink.

353
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,960
Ink?

354
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,080
Um...

355
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:49,520
What food do you like?

356
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:50,480
My treat next time.

357
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:52,120
That's enough.

358
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:52,960
Nice try.

359
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:55,200
Go hit on someone else.

360
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,360
That trick is so outdated.

361
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,800
Ink, wait.

362
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:00,280
I really want to get to know you.

363
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,800
You seem really nice

364
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:05,040
and cute.

365
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:06,800
I'll admit,

366
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:09,080
I'm not good at flirting, but...

367
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:11,000
Just go.

368
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:13,200
I'm screwed.

369
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:14,520
Besides,

370
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,440
my friend just died.

371
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:19,160
I'm not in the mood
for your stupid games.

372
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:38,640
Thank you so much.

373
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:42,600
See you around.

374
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,240
Thank you so much.

375
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,440
You look cute in glasses.

376
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,440
None of your business.

377
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,920
Look what I got.

378
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,480
To run a DNA test on hair,

379
00:23:18,560 --> 00:23:20,120
we need the hair follicle.

380
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,640
I know that.

381
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:24,880
I checked. It's still attached.

382
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:27,840
By the way,

383
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,840
How are you so hopeless with tech?

384
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,840
We almost had to go back empty-handed.

385
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:33,560
How do I use this?

386
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:35,280
Use what?

387
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,160
This?

388
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:38,600
I want a phone like this.

389
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,800
How does it work?

390
00:23:43,840 --> 00:23:46,360
It's called a smartphone, Inspector.

391
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:49,040
It can take pictures too.

392
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:50,760
Come closer and look.

393
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:09,640
Inspector.

394
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:11,960
Come here.

395
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,600
Just come here.

396
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:18,040
Got you something.

397
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:32,880
Here.

398
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,400
You wanted one, right?

399
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:50,360
I set up a new eSIM for you.

400
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,520
I wasn't sure if your current SIM

401
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:53,880
was a Nano SIM.

402
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:55,920
When you get a chance

403
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:57,960
swap it for a new one and pop it in.

404
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,360
I also installed

405
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:12,320
these social media apps

406
00:25:12,800 --> 00:25:14,240
for you.

407
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:16,760
Use them to look things up.

408
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:18,440
There's lots

409
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:20,560
of information on here.

410
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:25,680
Why would anyone put their life

411
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:27,800
out there like this,

412
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:29,880
with no concern for privacy?

413
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,600
Most people are like that.

414
00:25:33,040 --> 00:25:34,240
You're the one

415
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:35,600
who's a little strange.

416
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:38,880
People will think you came
from the Stone Age.

417
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:42,600
I'm kidding.

418
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,560
Keep scrolling.

419
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,360
Check this out.

420
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:05,960
Let me see.

421
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:16,440
What're you doing?

422
00:26:23,680 --> 00:26:24,360
Here.

423
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:31,440
I just saved a few things for you.

424
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,200
Or would you rather do it yourself?

425
00:26:40,360 --> 00:26:41,560
What are you doing?

426
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:42,720
Turn it off.

427
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:43,720
Turn it off.

428
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:45,160
- Turn it off.
- How?

429
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:50,320
Not like that.

430
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:52,040
Move your hand! Move!

431
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,840
There, it's off.

432
00:26:58,600 --> 00:27:00,560
Play around with it when you're free.

433
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:01,520
I'm heading off.

434
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,280
When testing DNA

435
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:34,880
from a victim's hair,

436
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:36,640
we don't test the hair itself.

437
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,280
We test the root.

438
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,560
Know why?

439
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:42,640
The root still has tissue
attached to it.

440
00:27:42,720 --> 00:27:45,200
That's where we extract the DNA.

441
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:47,120
See?

442
00:28:00,240 --> 00:28:01,280
Come in.

443
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:03,120
Doctor.

444
00:28:03,120 --> 00:28:04,080
The results are in.

445
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:05,040
Thanks.

446
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,520
Inspector Ken.

447
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:30,040
What are you reading?

448
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:33,320
A DNA report.

449
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:34,080
Is it Ink's?

450
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:38,480
Ink isn't the killer.

451
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:41,280
Besides, I've already told you

452
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:43,880
not to barge in here.

453
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,200
Inspector.

454
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,320
We're investigating the same case.

455
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:50,760
We should share

456
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:52,120
any information we find.

457
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:54,760
Be my guest.

458
00:28:58,400 --> 00:28:59,480
Before I go,

459
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:01,040
where's your phone?

460
00:29:07,920 --> 00:29:08,920
See? It's not lost.

461
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:11,800
Learn how to use it next time,

462
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:14,000
so I don't have to come all this way.

463
00:29:14,520 --> 00:29:15,360
Got it?

464
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:18,560
Go ahead.

465
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,320
I'm getting back to the case.

466
00:29:45,440 --> 00:29:46,160
Inspector.

467
00:29:51,560 --> 00:29:53,200
Do you ever answer your phone?

468
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,160
How did you know I was here?

469
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:01,600
It's called Find My.

470
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:03,880
That's technology for you.

471
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,560
Wait.

472
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:10,040
Give it a chance, Inspector.

473
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:14,960
I thought

474
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:18,840
you'd slipped away to investigate alone.

475
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:20,880
By the way,

476
00:30:22,080 --> 00:30:23,160
what's here?

477
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:24,200
It's pretty nice.

478
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:27,040
I came here to unwind.

479
00:30:31,280 --> 00:30:32,040
So, after

480
00:30:32,760 --> 00:30:34,960
staring at red blood all day,

481
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:36,920
doctors come here to see green?

482
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:39,840
I'm color-blind to red.

483
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:41,920
I see.

484
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:45,720
Um...

485
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:47,760
Those photos

486
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:50,880
we saw at the library...

487
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:53,440
how do I see them?

488
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:56,480
On social media?

489
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:02,560
I installed the apps for you.

490
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:05,560
What's the victim's account?

491
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:10,080
What's this?

492
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:13,320
Highlights.

493
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:22,480
Inspector.

494
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:25,520
There's someone else
we need to look into.

495
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:32,960
Put it on speaker.

496
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:35,240
- Go ahead.
- I learned something.

497
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:36,760
The DNA

498
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,120
isn't a match for Ping.

499
00:31:39,680 --> 00:31:40,320
And

500
00:31:42,240 --> 00:31:45,040
the blood isn't hers either.
Even the type is different.

501
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:48,960
You should head home.

502
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,240
Tee can check on him.

503
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:52,080
It's late.

504
00:31:52,440 --> 00:31:53,440
What do you mean?

505
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:55,240
You guys aren't going home?

506
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:56,360
Uh...

507
00:31:58,400 --> 00:32:00,120
Inspector.

508
00:32:00,600 --> 00:32:02,080
What's wrong?

509
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:11,840
This man...

510
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:12,840
is he your friend?

511
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:14,840
Oh.

512
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:15,960
Where is he now?

513
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:17,640
Tee?

514
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:19,600
What is it, Inspector?

515
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,280
We just want to talk to him.

516
00:32:23,520 --> 00:32:25,200
Do you suspect Tee?

517
00:32:26,120 --> 00:32:28,000
Tee couldn't have done it.

518
00:32:28,520 --> 00:32:29,120
Because...

519
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:31,000
He was there when it happened,

520
00:32:31,080 --> 00:32:32,040
but he was with his girlfriend.

521
00:32:33,480 --> 00:32:34,360
Either way,

522
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:36,040
we still need to question him.

523
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:37,600
He may know something.

524
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:38,880
I see.

525
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:40,640
Sure.

526
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:42,080
But he's sick.

527
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:43,440
He's still in bed.

528
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:45,040
We were about to visit him.

529
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,320
Look at Tee.

530
00:32:47,520 --> 00:32:49,000
He couldn't hurt anyone.

531
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:50,280
He's skinny as a stick.

532
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:52,240
He isn't a suspect yet.

533
00:32:52,320 --> 00:32:53,400
We just want to talk.

534
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:55,400
Look.

535
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:56,520
Tee.

536
00:32:57,400 --> 00:32:57,960
Look.

537
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:59,560
The inspectors want to talk to you.

538
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:01,400
Has your fever broken?

539
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:02,960
Yeah, I'm much better.

540
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,160
Good, good.

541
00:33:04,560 --> 00:33:05,880
Then you...

542
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:07,000
Hey.

543
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:08,800
Hey!

544
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:10,640
No, stay in your room.

545
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,640
Hey! Stop!

546
00:33:20,320 --> 00:33:21,280
Go around that way.

547
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:22,080
I'll go this way.

548
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:38,080
- Hey.
- This road sucks.

549
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:17,680
Hey!

550
00:34:17,920 --> 00:34:18,840
It's me.

551
00:34:20,280 --> 00:34:21,320
Tee, he...

552
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:23,120
Hey! Watch out!

553
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:39,160
I told you to go after him!

554
00:34:39,200 --> 00:34:39,960
No.

555
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:42,040
Hey.

556
00:34:42,640 --> 00:34:43,640
Are you okay?

557
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:48,200
Hey.

558
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:51,240
What are you looking at?

559
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:53,800
It's just a scratch.
I'll get it checked out myself.

560
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:55,360
I am a doctor.

561
00:34:56,200 --> 00:34:56,960
Shut up.

562
00:34:57,240 --> 00:34:58,040
Come here.

563
00:35:01,480 --> 00:35:02,200
Get up.

564
00:35:03,600 --> 00:35:04,440
Ow.

565
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:08,840
Come here.

566
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:26,160
Shirt off.

567
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:26,960
You need stitches.

568
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:28,360
Do I really need stitches?

569
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,200
Shirt off.

570
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,360
Take it off, or I'll cut it off.

571
00:35:34,360 --> 00:35:35,720
Hold on.

572
00:35:42,040 --> 00:35:42,880
Ow, that hurts.

573
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:48,280
Easy.

574
00:35:51,200 --> 00:35:52,120
Is it bad?

575
00:35:57,640 --> 00:35:58,520
That's it.

576
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:05,400
This won't hurt.

577
00:36:06,080 --> 00:36:07,080
Don't move.

578
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,160
It gets easier.

579
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:18,440
Why didn't you take me to a doctor?

580
00:36:21,640 --> 00:36:22,800
Didn't I tell you?

581
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:23,760
I am a doctor.

582
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,560
Then why did you save me?

583
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:29,400
Why not go after him?

584
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:32,840
Because you saved me.

585
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:39,000
You know,

586
